INT. FERRYBOAT SNACK BAR - AFTERNOON

Plastic chairs bolted down. Gulls wheel past the window. GRANDPA EZEKIEL (70s, cardigan, newspaper folded in quarters) stirs his coffee while his granddaughter PIPPA (9, bandaged knee, sticker book) turns pages beside him and her older brother JUNIOR (14, hood up, one earbud in) slouches opposite, ignoring both and sliding his sandwich crust from one side of the plate to the other.

                    PIPPA
          Grandpa, did you ever fall off a boat?

                    EZEKIEL
          Twice.

                    PIPPA
          Did it hurt?

                    EZEKIEL
          The second time, no. By then I knew how.

                    JUNIOR
          That's not how that works.

                    EZEKIEL
          It is if you do it right.

                    PIPPA
          Show me.

                    EZEKIEL
          Not on this boat.

                    JUNIOR
          Can we get off at the next stop?

                    EZEKIEL
          There's no next stop. It's a ferry.

                    PIPPA
          Then we're stuck.

                    EZEKIEL
          Stuck is a strong word. We're simply committed.
